## Constraints & Assumptions

- **C-01**: Language for the agent script — the repo has Python (`app/`) and TypeScript (`infra/`). Assumption: the agent will be implemented in **Python** (consistent with existing app + Hypothesis for PBT), to be confirmed in NFR Requirements/tech-stack stage.
- **C-02**: The GitHub repo already has an OIDC provider + `GitHubActionsDeployRole`. Bedrock permissions will be added via least-privilege — either to a new dedicated role or a scoped policy (decided in Infrastructure Design).
- **C-03**: The existing branch protection on `dev`/`main` must be configured to require the new status check for FR-06 to actually block merges (a repo settings step — documented, not code).
- **C-04**: Bedrock model availability in `us-east-1` (the region used by the existing pipeline) is assumed.

---

## Key Requirements Summary

The feature adds an autonomous, Bedrock-powered code reviewer that runs as a new GitHub Actions workflow (on the existing CodeBuild runner) for every PR to `dev`. It reviews quality, correctness, and security; posts summary + inline comments; **blocks merge via a required status check on high-severity findings**; and **auto-approves** clean PRs. Security Baseline and (full) Property-Based Testing extensions are enforced as blocking constraints; Resiliency is opt-out.

